<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hine E Hine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1907</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Hine E Hine&quot; is a lullaby in Māori written in around 1907 by Fanny Howie, who performed under the stage name Princess Te Rangi Pai. It was published in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> by Beal, Stuttard &amp; Co., around 1914, as &quot;A Maori Slumber <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> – Hine E Hine&quot;, under her stage name; a copy is held by the Alexander Turnbull Library of the National Library of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>.</p></div>
